Set the two parameters of the rule “accelerate right if \(v + \theta_1 x + \theta_2 &gt; 0\)” and watch ten cars (starting at rest between \(x = -0.6\) and \(-0.4\)) try to escape. The map shows the average number of steps for every parameter pair. The white area is the plateau where no car escapes within 200 steps, and your policy is the orange dot. Try to find the narrow diagonal ridge of good policies, and notice how little changes as you move around on the plateau.

